1. She is a British VTuber with a celestial messenger origin story. (Verbatim: "I'm a celestial messenger that got hit by a truck and got isekhied and became British.")
2. Her lore involves a reverse isekai where she was reborn as a British person. (Verbatim: "It's technically a reverse isekai, because where the heck is the isekai where you get reborn as a British?")
3. She has wings but is unable to fly due to fear and lack of a flying license. (Verbatim: "I do have wings, technically. Which I hear, but I'm too scared to use them.")
4. She is scared of butterflies and other flying things, possibly due to bright-colored accessories. (Verbatim: "I'm normally scared of butterflies and any flying things. But I think it might be because I normally like to have bright colored scrunchies and stuff.")
5. She has a fondness for roses and remembers a rose arch from her childhood garden. (Verbatim: "We had this rose arch in the garden. And I always told myself if I was to ever get my own place and a garden, I would want to get a rose arch.")
6. She enjoys gardening and remembers helping water plants in her parents' garden. (Verbatim: "I used to help water them.")
7. She plans to buy discounted British chocolate on a future visit to a shop. (Verbatim: "Tomorrow, I'm very excited to go to the shop and get all the discounted British chocolate.")
8. Her birthday is on March 7th. (Verbatim: "It's not my birthday either. It's not until the 7th of March, okay?")
9. She is currently experiencing jet lag from traveling to England. (Verbatim: "But jet lag is hitting us hard, isn't it?")
10. She values the emotional energy and support she receives from her audience, stating she reflects their light. (Verbatim: "I'm only bright because I reflect the light that you all give me.") [end of text]



1. She attended a Roman Catholic school during her education. (Verbatim: "like and that was the only time i've ever been able to help out a team at a pub quiz so another free super view is not free i love you thank you so much for all the smiles every time you go live i smile just the thought of the laughs will all have together have an amazing to me i hope i hope i can make people laugh a little bit or smile just a little smile just a little relief on the heart you know we're all here having a good time together yeah yeah yeah yeah uh roman catholic nana ellie is very roman catholic so i had to go to a catholic school and i was made to go to the roman catholic church every sunday")
2. She was required to attend Roman Catholic Church services every Sunday as a child. (Verbatim: "i had to go to a catholic school and i was made to go to the roman catholic church every sunday")
3. She has a strong dislike for loud, chaotic environments such as noisy bars. (Verbatim: "luckily this bar is really quiet to be honest because bars are kind of scary right i remember the first time i walked into an english pub and i i died inside and outside it was terrifying there were so many people and i was just like nope nope nope nope nope nope nope you know")
4. She finds pub quizzes intimidating due to her lack of general knowledge, music, and sports knowledge. (Verbatim: "in terms of a pub quiz like contestant you wouldn't want me on your team and when i was a student i helped with one quiz okay there i remember this very clearly this is a core memory where i actually managed to help one time and it was only because for some reason one question in this pub quiz was related to the bible and i was like i know this i went to catholic school")
5. She once created and hosted a McDonald's-themed quiz at work, which became so frequent that her coworkers asked her to stop. (Verbatim: "when it was my turn i did a quiz on mcdonald's i did geogaster mcdonald's and had them guess which mcdonald's which country the mcdonald's was in and then the next time it was my turn i did another one on mcdonald's and this time i did it on um mcdonald's food items and which country they're sold in and then they stopped letting me have a turn because they said that i should stop doing mcdonald's themed quizzes but i thought they were good")
6. She has a fond memory of a student bar that served a drink called "Mad Hatter's Tea Party" with green tea. (Verbatim: "oh no no no no no no not absent no absolutely not i remember at uni they had like okay drinking culture is very big in england okay and they'd have like these like student places and i remember one of them served this drink and it was apparently so awful like it literally had i feel like it just listed every possible alcohol and then just like shoved it into this scary looking cup and and they were like only only one allowed per person and i was like what the heck is this thing i never tried it because it scared the heck out of me and it had some kind of terrifying name but irish cream with bananas okay that doesn't sound too bad but yo tea party sounds nice though i like the idea of a tea something in a teapot")
7. She has a preference for cozy, quiet, and cute environments over loud or crowded ones. (Verbatim: "i much prefer somewhere comfy cozy and cute like here you know")
8. She once helped with a pub quiz during her university years, succeeding only because of her Catholic school education. (Verbatim: "when i was a student i helped with one quiz okay there i remember this very clearly this is a core memory where i actually managed to help one time and it was only because for some reason one question in this pub quiz was related to the bible and i was like i know this i went to catholic school")
9. She is not currently required to attend church, having chosen to stop after becoming an adult. (Verbatim: "can't confirm i don't have to go anymore as soon as i became an adult they were like you can choose and i was like okay bye they were so mad no it's")
10. She has a fondness for the idea of themed tea parties, particularly ones with a whimsical or fantasy aesthetic. (Verbatim: "yo tea party sounds nice though i like the idea of a tea something in a teapot") [end of text]



1. She identifies her personal philosophy as "just be a good person" and considers this her guiding principle. (Verbatim: "like oh no wait we haven't supposed to be in the onsen okay i'm just getting changed okay... just be a good person i that that that is my religion just be a good person")
2. She was raised in a Roman Catholic household but stopped attending church after becoming an adult. (Verbatim: "the roman catholic church every sunday um can't confirm i don't have to go anymore as soon as i became an adult they were like you can choose")
3. She visited Japan and stayed in a traditional onsen town called Kinosaki. (Verbatim: "i went to an onsen town called kinosaki i highly recommend kinosaki it's also very welcoming to foreigners")
4. She has a long neck, which she attributes to natural anatomy rather than being a goose. (Verbatim: "i do have a long neck it's not because i'm a goose though um i was just born with it")
5. She recommends visiting Kinosaki Onsen town in Japan for its welcoming attitude toward foreigners, especially those with tattoos. (Verbatim: "apparently kinosaki is special in a sense that if you have tattoos you can still go to every single onsen in that little town")
6. She enjoys the experience of walking around in a yukata and wooden slippers in an onsen town. (Verbatim: "you get the clippy clippy clippy wooden slippers and it's so nice like it just it just feels like such a magical place")
7. She values the contrast between hot and cold baths for relaxation. (Verbatim: "what i like to do is hop between the hot and the cold baths um yeah yeah kinosaki is quite far to get to though")
8. She found the onsen experience deeply relaxing and emotionally releasing. (Verbatim: "i was absolutely like what you call it just blown away by how relaxing it was and that i didn't realize how much stress i was holding on to until i was in that little onsen bath and was like i don't know i wanted to just break down i was just so like relaxed")
9. She enjoys eating ice cream after soaking in an onsen. (Verbatim: "oh and i had ice cream i had ice cream i remember i got out the onsen put on my yukata walked over and was like yeah like yeah ice cream ice cream and it felt it tasted so good")
10. She has a fictional connection to the celestial realm, where the onsen in the stream is located. (Verbatim: "this onsen is in the celestial realm that got copied from earth so i don't know about the time of year or anything because nothing makes sense") [end of text]



1. She is British. (Verbatim: "but i'm just british um")  
2. She struggles with expressing emotions in words. (Verbatim: "i wish i wish i could write in words better and then i could write you guys a nice valentine's thing but words really aren't my forte")  
3. She grew up in a household that never discussed feelings. (Verbatim: "especially since i grew up in a household that does not talk about feelings in the slightest ever")  
4. She feels a constant pressure to do more and fears not being enough. (Verbatim: "i always feel like i'm not doing enough i always feel i have a permanent feeling of i'm not doing enough")  
5. She finds it difficult to maintain confidence in her VTuber identity due to comparison with others. (Verbatim: "it's like an you're constantly compared and you know people come and go and stuff and it's scary")  
6. She values emotional connection and support from her audience deeply. (Verbatim: "you guys always manage to make me feel special so thank you for doing that")  
7. She enjoys roleplay but admits she's not very good at it yet. (Verbatim: "I'm still not very good at this whole role play thing but I'm working on it")  
8. She finds comfort in games like Final Fantasy 14 as a form of escape. (Verbatim: "I think that's why I love games like Final Fantasy 14 and stuff ones where you can really just dive in and and escape")  
9. She values relaxation and mental well-being, especially during stressful times. (Verbatim: "my thought process was to do something nice and relaxing for those that are feeling extremely stressed")  
10. She views her VTuber role as a way to bring happiness to others, not stress. (Verbatim: "we're vtubers to make people happy and that's that's what i want to try and do") [end of text]



